**Definition 11.4 (comparison with simpler interfaces).** The choices
have the following demonstrated relations, rather than a scalar ranking.

| Candidate | Proven relation and actual boundary |
| --- | --- |
| Supplied native Image only | Actual paid recovery/current checker already exists, but no natural body is output or consumed. It leaves this interface gap. |
| One selectable natural body or one four-body bundle | Can satisfy their stated immediate-decoder tasks; does not itself execute this requested receiver-to-receiver fixed cycle. No inferiority claim is made. |
| This five-publication cycle | Each arrow consumes the previous receiver's single body and the final checker compares two received S bodies. It incurs five full added publications and all enlarged-code/bank work. |
| Four-publication cycle with local starting S | Can close a cycle whose initial S is local bank data. It omits one actual starting-S delivery required by the chosen received-body contract. |
| Registry-based later Convert API | Requires real lookup, acquired identifiers, bindings and its own input/progress proof. No present client here requests independent later lookup; deleting that registry does not break the fixed chain's acquired data dependency. |
| Native-row T checker versus general virtual graph store | Lemma 5.4 gives equality only on canonical row-lift images. Both need their complete actual code/cost account for a price comparison. |
| Absolute paths versus compact masks/contours | Proposition 4.2 proves the codec-class quadratic obligation; Proposition 4.1 gives exact compact geometric lengths. This compares wire bodies, not complete native costs. |
| New annex or occupied-lane overlay | An annex would need paid extra boundaries/owners/Step/catalog and transfer; no necessity is proved. Literal overlay on occupied verifier lanes has the supplied grammar/authority mismatch. |

No minimum-role, optimal-codec, total-price dominance, physical duration/
energy or infinite-progress assertion is made. Extra code/register fields
can increase every earlier bank rebuild as well as new work; copy/print
savings alone cannot settle a whole-run comparison.

